Game Boy Pokémon companion data (the kiwami fork of BananaOS)

The *.ram.json files in this folder hold what the companion on the game panel reads from Pokémon Red, Blue, Yellow,
Gold, Silver and Crystal while they play: the RAM addresses of the party, the bag, the battle and the rest, and the
releases' SHA-1s. They are extracted from PokeDaisy by the fork's kiwami/tools/pokedaisy-extract.py, merged with
addresses, ROM offsets and constants from pret's disassemblies (pokecrystal, pokegold, pokered, pokeyellow), which
publish no license, taken by kiwami/tools/pret-extract.py as facts about the retail ROMs. SOURCES names the commits
read and the SHA-256 of every file read and written. Nothing of the games themselves (their names, text, pictures or
tables) is here: the companion reads those from the player's own ROM while it runs.

